# Configuration template. Two ways to supply real credentials:
#
#   PREFERRED: keep keys in ONE private file outside every repo, e.g.
#   ~/.secrets/ai.env (chmod 600), and point ENV_FILE at it per run:
#       ENV_FILE=~/.secrets/ai.env AGENT_PROVIDER=anthropic npm run demo
#       ENV_FILE=~/.secrets/ai.env AGENT_PROVIDER=openai    npm run demo
#   Keys never appear in commands, shell history, or the repo.
#
#   ALTERNATIVE: cp .env.example .env and fill it in. NEVER commit .env.
#
# With no provider configured the service runs the deterministic offline mock.

# mock | anthropic | openai
AGENT_PROVIDER=mock

# Required only for the matching provider:
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
# ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5
# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...
# OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-4o

# PORT=3000
# HOST=127.0.0.1
# LOG_LEVEL=info
# MAX_TOOL_ITERATIONS=5
# MAX_TOKENS=1024
# REQUEST_TIMEOUT_MS=120000
